{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"55070","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55070","key":"SV-8936","renderedFields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"Today 10:27 AM","issuetype":null,"timespent":null,"project":null,"customfield_10351":"","fixVersions":null,"aggregatetimespent":null,"statusCategory":null,"resolution":null,"resolutiondate":null,"workratio":null,"watches":null,"issuerestriction":null,"lastViewed":null,"created":"Today 10:27 AM","customfield_10021":null,"customfield_10385":null,"priority":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10016":null,"customfield_10019":null,"timeestimate":null,"aggregatetimeoriginalestimate":null,"versions":null,"customfield_10418":null,"customfield_10419":null,"issuelinks":null,"assignee":null,"updated":"Today 12:49 PM","status":null,"components":null,"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"1.Whathappensnow\"></a>1. What happens now</h3>\n\n<p>When a download from the Parts Velocity report finishes, the message that pops up reads \"Success - Data exported successfully.\" That is a general message that could belong to any screen in the application; it does not name the report or say which of the two files was produced.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"2.Whatshouldhappeninstead\"></a>2. What should happen instead</h3>\n\n<p>The written description sets the exact wording, and it names both the report and the file type.</p>\n\n<p>Parts Velocity specification, version 5, requirement S6-R9: \"On a successful download, a success toast reads \\\"Velocity report exported (CSV)\\\" or \\\"Velocity report exported (PDF)\\\".\"</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"3.Howtoseeit\"></a>3. How to see it</h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Sign in as a user who can see reports and open <b>Reports</b> &gt; <b>Parts Velocity</b>.</li>\n\t<li>In the report's own search box type <b>BRAKECLEAN</b>, so the view is small enough to download.</li>\n\t<li>Open the three-dot menu at the top of the report and choose <b>Download (CSV)</b>. Watch the message that appears.</li>\n\t<li>Do it again and choose <b>Download (PDF)</b>. Watch the message that appears.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>Exact test data this was seen with:</b> part number <b>BRAKECLEAN</b>, locations <b>Staging Heavy Duty - 9919</b> and <b>Staging Lethbridge - 4310</b>, date range <b>This Year</b>, type <b>Both</b>.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"4.Whatwasactuallyshown\"></a>4. What was actually shown</h3>\n\n<p>Both downloads showed the same message:</p>\n\n{noquote}<br/>\nSuccess<br/>\nData exported successfully.{noquote}\n\n<p>The expected messages were <tt>Velocity report exported (CSV)</tt> and <tt>Velocity report exported (PDF)</tt>.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"5.Whatwasruledout\"></a>5. What was ruled out</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><b>It is not a missing message.</b> A message does appear, and it appears for both file types - it is the wording that is wrong.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not the failure message.</b> The failure message is correct: when a download is refused, the message the server sends is passed through and shown to the user word for word, which is what the written description asks for.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not one file type.</b> The spreadsheet and the PDF both show the same general wording.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not a timing problem.</b> The message was captured as it appeared, on four separate downloads.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"6.Howoften\"></a>6. How often</h3>\n\n<p>Every time. Four downloads out of four.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"7.Whereitwasseen\"></a>7. Where it was seen</h3>\n\n<p>Reports &gt; Parts Velocity, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Parts Velocity report specification, version 5, requirement S6-R9, which says: \"On a successful download, a success toast reads “Velocity report exported (CSV)” or “Velocity report exported (PDF)”.\" The wording names the report and the file type, which the general message does not.</p>","customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[],"summary":null,"creator":null,"subtasks":null,"customfield_10285":"","reporter":null,"customfield_10044":null,"aggregateprogress":null,"customfield_10046":null,"customfield_10047":null,"environment":"","customfield_10318":null,"duedate":null,"customfield_10518":null,"progress":null,"votes":null,"comment":{"comments":[],"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55070/comment","maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"worklog":{"startAt":0,"maxResults":20,"total":0,"worklogs":[]}},"fields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"2026-08-06T00:27:20.576-0500","issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10007","id":"10007","description":"Subtasks track small pieces of work that are part of a larger task. (Migrated on 31 Dec 2023 09:01 UTC)","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10854?size=medium","name":"Story Defect","subtask":true,"avatarId":10854,"entityId":"0900502c-ae66-465f-a9da-8322307b07ff","hierarchyLevel":-1},"parent":{"id":"54667","key":"SV-8646","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/54667","fields":{"summary":"Velocity - Story 6 - Exports (CSV & PDF)","status":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/status/10349","description":"","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/","name":"Open","id":"10349","statusCategory":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/statuscategory/2","id":2,"key":"new","colorName":"blue-gray","name":"To Do"}},"priority":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/priority/3","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/medium_new.svg","name":"Medium","id":"3"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10245","id":"10245","description":"Stories track functionality or features expressed as user goals.","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/